course: dictionary
lesson: 1331
title: What is a calorie?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A calorie is a unit, a way of measuring. It tells you how much energy food gives your body. «Moving and keeping warm in cool water use lots of energy, and food labels count that energy, often in calories.» Just as a metre measures length, a calorie measures energy.
explain: Your body uses energy to move, grow and keep warm, and that energy comes from food. So the calories on a label tell you how much energy the food will give you. «Rice, wheat and maize together provide a large share of all the calories people eat in the world.» Here calories means the energy people get from food.
explain: Use the context to work out the meaning. Words like «energy», «food» and «labels» are clues. Then check by putting your meaning into the sentence: does «food labels count how much energy the food gives» still make sense? If it does, you are right.
fact: A calorie is a unit used to measure energy.
fact: In science, a calorie is a small unit of heat energy.
fact: On food labels the number is usually given in kilocalories (kcal), and one kilocalorie is 1,000 small calories.
fact: Children need enough calories to grow, but pupils learn about balance rather than counting every calorie.
fact: «Calorie» is a noun: a calorie, calories.
exercise: «Moving and keeping warm in cool water use lots of energy.» What is a calorie? | *A unit used to measure energy from food | A tool for weighing people | A type of bread | A kind of cold water
exercise: Where might you find calories on a packet of food? | *On the food label, often shown as kcal | On the bottom of your shoe | Spread across the table | Inside the school library
exercise: «Rice, wheat and maize together provide a large share of all the calories people eat in the world.» Find and copy one word that means a part of the total. | maize | calories | world | *share
test: What do calories tell us about food? | How long it stays fresh | *How much energy it gives the body | How heavy the food is | What colour it is
test: Why does your body need calories? | To change colour | *To move, grow and keep warm | To read books | To make food taste sweet
exam: A label says 200 kcal. What does this tell you? | The food has 200 pieces | The food weighs 200 grams | *The food gives the body 200 kilocalories of energy | The food costs 200 pence
